---
pagination: { data: languages, size: 1, alias: lang }
permalink: "{{ '/' if lang == 'en' else '/es/' }}events/index.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: events
titleKey: nav.events
ldType: CollectionPage
descKey: committee.events.meta_desc
pageScripts: ["/assets/js/committee.js"]
# the calendar file of this page's events (src/pages/events-ics.11ty.js), named in the page's <head> (base.njk)
calendarFeed: "/events.ics"
---
{#- Events: committee meetings (computed), monthly recurring events (config/site.yml `recurring_events:` — one
    La Viña holds — `host: lv`, its monthly workshop on Zoom — is with the GV & LV calendars, in La Viña's colour,
    online only: "Online on Zoom", Join online, its meeting ID; our own Grapevine Meeting is a NETA 65 one — its
    badge says so, never Grapevine's —, online only: "Online on Google Meet", its meeting code), Drive flyers with
    dated names, manual events, Texas GV/LV calendar events (a date we already show is left out by build_data).
    Since round 30 EVERY date to come is a card of its own — a monthly series' every date, every committee meeting
    (no "Show every monthly date" switch, no "Then …" line). Grouped by month, filterable, with a row of month chips
    and per-event calendar buttons. On top, whatever the filter, "Our monthly meetings" (#ev-pinned): the next
    committee meeting and the next Grapevine Meeting, then the weekly open meetings (#ev-weekly), then the months,
    by whole years: the rest of the build's year open and, from November on, all of the next year too (built in
    November 2026: through December 2027, all of 2027); the later years (all of 2028) folded behind "Show 2028 dates
    (n)" (committee.js eventsFold, cmEvents).
    Below the shared page hero: the agenda (then "how events get here", the three kinds of events in
    visitors' words) and, from 1024px, a sidebar: the .ics subscription card (#subscribe), then the "Next 5 weeks"
    calendar (#ev-cal), which stays in view under the header while the list scrolls (its sticky-aside wrapper);
    below 1024px both follow the agenda. Last, collapsed, "For committee members · Add an event"
    (ui.memberHelp, #how-events): the two kinds of flyers (a dated name makes an event; the flyer of an
    event written in content/events has an undated name and is linked with `flyer:`), the Drive folder,
    the flyer naming rule + examples, and the Portfolio's two Drive actions. With no NETA 65 events, the
    agenda's empty slot (#ev-empty-neta) points there.
    The hero's right-hand card (the shared hero aside, "Save the date"): the next Area assembly (event-tone.js
    isAssembly: never an ACM or a town hall) — else the next event from Grapevine's or La Viña's own calendars —
    never the first one-off event of the list below; its link goes to that event in the list. Hidden on smaller
    screens and at larger text (the committee sub-nav stays right under the hero, and the event is in the list). -#}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{%- set all = db.events.items | cmEvents(site, lang) | cmCollapseRecurring -%}
{%- set upcoming = all | where("past", false) -%}
{#- Past list: real one-off events only (a monthly meeting / booth date that has passed is not news — so
    the calendar entry of such a date links to this page itself, not to a card: committee.js detailsUrl) -#}
{%- set past = all | where("past", true) | whereNot("committee", true) | whereNot("recurring", true) | reverse -%}
{%- set meetings = upcoming | where("committee", true) -%}
{%- set next = meetings[0] -%}
{#- Counts = what each filter chip shows: every card — a monthly series' every date, the folded months' too (they are
    a click away); committee.js recounts after hiding events that have passed. The committee meetings; the NETA 65
    events — ours AND the committee meetings, which are NETA 65 events too (their cards' data-group="committee
    neta"); the GV & LV calendars. nNetaOwn — our NETA 65 events without the committee meetings — keeps its own
    meaning: no flyer or event of ours yet (the empty state #ev-empty-neta, cmDriveChecked). -#}
{%- set nNetaOwn = upcoming | where("group", "neta") | length -%}
{%- set nNeta = nNetaOwn + meetings.length -%}
{%- set nCal = upcoming | where("group", "calendar") | length -%}
{%- set pageAbs = page.url | siteUrl(site) -%}
{%- set m = site.meeting -%}
{#- where the committee meeting is held, in the page's words ("Join on Zoom"): config/site.yml meeting.platform -#}
{%- set pf = { platform: m.platform or "Zoom" } -%}
{%- set di = db.status | cmDriveInfo(site) -%}

{#- The kind of an event, in words and in its colour (eventTone: eleventy/filters/event-tone.js; the
    colours are the .ev-tone-* rules in committee.css). The card carries .ev-tone-<kind>; this badge
    names the kind, so the colour is never the only signal. An event from Grapevine's or La Viña's own
    calendar keeps saying so ("La Viña calendar"). The Area's own events (an assembly, an ACM, the Area's town
    hall) share one colour, "Area event"; an assembly itself says "Area assembly" (event-tone.js isAssembly). -#}
{% macro kindBadge(ev, kind) %}
{%- set kindIcon = { committee: "users", gv: "grapes", lv: "grapes", booth: "store", assembly: "landmark", other: "map-pin" } -%}
{%- if kind == "gv" and ev.category == "gv-calendar" %}{% set label = "committee.events.badge_gv" | t(lang) %}
{%- elif kind == "lv" and ev.category == "lv-calendar" %}{% set label = "committee.events.badge_lv" | t(lang) %}
{%- elif kind == "assembly" %}{% set label = ("committee.events.badge_assembly" if (ev | isAssembly) else "committee.events.kind.assembly") | t(lang) %}
{%- elif kind == "other" %}{% set label = ("committee.events.kind.neta" if ev.group == "neta" else "committee.events.kind.event") | t(lang) %}
{%- else %}{% set label = ("committee.events.kind." + kind) | t(lang) %}{% endif -%}
{#- (our Grapevine Meeting: "NETA 65" — event-tone.js gives a meeting series of ours no magazine's colour —, online
    only: the camera, not the map pin) -#}
{%- set ico = "video" if (kind == "other" and ev.isOnline and not ev.location) else kindIcon[kind] -%}
<span class="badge ev-badge">{% icon ico, "size-3" %} {{ label }}</span>
{%- endmacro %}

{#- "Add to calendar" dropdown (Google / Outlook links work without JS; .ics download needs JS) -#}
{% macro calMenu(ev, dark=false) %}
<details class="cm-menu">
  {#- phones: the short visible label ("Calendar"), the full one for screen readers -#}
  <summary class="{{ 'btn-on-dark' if dark else 'btn-secondary' }} btn-sm">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.cal_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</span></summary>
  <div class="cm-menu-panel">
    <a href="{{ ev.gcal }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar</a>
    <a href="{{ ev.outlook }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Outlook.com</a>
    <button type="button" data-cm-ics="{{ ev.icsData | json }}" data-cm-js>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</button>
    <p class="cm-menu-note" data-cm-js>{{ ("committee.cal.reminder_day" if ev.allDay else "committee.cal.reminder_timed") | t(lang) }}</p>
  </div>
</details>
{% endmacro %}

{#- "Save the date": from the events with a date of their own (no committee meetings, a monthly series by its next
    date: cmCollapseRecurring's `later`), skipping the first of them — that one is near the top of the list anyway;
    the next Area ASSEMBLY (isAssembly: an ACM or the Area's town hall shares its colour but is not one) -#}
{%- set ahead = upcoming | whereNot("committee", true) | whereNot("later", true) -%}
{%- set sdPick = [] -%}
{%- for ev in ahead %}{% if loop.index0 > 0 and not sdPick.length and (ev | isAssembly) and sdPick.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- for ev in ahead %}{% if loop.index0 > 0 and not sdPick.length and (ev.category == "gv-calendar" or ev.category == "lv-calendar") and sdPick.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set sd = sdPick[0] -%}
{% call(slot) ui.pageHero(lang, "nav.events" | t(lang), "committee.events.hero_sub" | t(lang), "calendar-days", "committee.events.eyebrow" | t(lang), { side: "hide" }) %}
{%- if slot == "side" %}
  {%- if sd %}
  {%- set sdKind = sd | eventTone %}
  {% call ui.heroAside("committee.events.aside_title" | t(lang), lang, { id: "ev-aside-title", icon: "calendar-heart", href: "#" + sd.anchor, linkLabel: "committee.events.aside_link" | t(lang) }) %}
  <div class="cm-ha-ev ev-tone-{{ sdKind }}">
    <span class="cm-ha-ev-tile{{ ' is-range' if sd.tile.range }}" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cm-tile-mon">{{ sd.tile.mon }}</span><span class="cm-ha-ev-day">{{ sd.tile.day }}</span><span class="cm-ha-ev-wd">{{ sd.tile.wd }}</span></span>
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p>{{ kindBadge(sd, sdKind) }}</p>
      <p class="hero-aside-title mt-1.5">{{ sd.title }}</p>
      <p class="hero-aside-text mt-0.5">{{ sd.rangeLabel if sd.multiDay else sd.shareWhen }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- else %}
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn-light" href="#subscribe">{% icon "calendar-sync", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.subscribe_btn" | t(lang) }}</a>
    <a class="btn-on-dark" href="{{ '/meetings/' | lurl(lang) }}#committee-meeting">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "nav.meeting" | t(lang) }}</a>
  </div>
  {#- No hero stat: the committee sub-nav's Events tab counts the upcoming events, each once (a monthly series
      once, no committee meetings: upcomingEventEnds); the filter chips count the cards — every date -#}
{%- endif %}
{% endcall %}

{% committeeNav lang, "events", db %}

<div class="container-page section pt-10 pb-0 sm:pt-12">
<div class="layout-aside">
<section class="min-w-0" x-data="cmEvents()" data-count-label="{{ 'committee.events.showing' | t(lang) }}" data-count-label-one="{{ 'committee.events.showing_one' | t(lang) }}" aria-labelledby="ev-upcoming-title">
  {{ ui.sectionHead("committee.events.upcoming" | t(lang), "committee.events.list_sub" | t(lang), "", "", "calendar-days", { eyebrow: "committee.events.list_eyebrow" | t(lang), tone: "text-vine", id: "ev-upcoming-title", lang: lang }) }}

  {#- ---------- Filter bar: one line of chips (it scrolls sideways on a phone); under it the months as
       jump chips (only the months with something showing) ---------- -#}
  {%- set months = upcoming | groupBy("monthKey") %}
  {#- The folded months (eventsFold: the years after the build's — after the next one from November on; all of
      2028 when built in November 2026 or in 2027 before November): their sections and jump chips carry data-cm-more and data-dflt-hidden — committee.css hides
      them from the first paint (with JavaScript), so nothing jumps when cmEvents starts; "Show {range} dates (n)"
      after the last open month shows them. fold = null: nothing folded, no button. -#}
  {%- set fold = upcoming | cmEventsFold -%}
  <div class="mb-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-3">
    <div class="chip-row" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.filter_aria' | t(lang) }}" data-js-only>
      {%- for f in [["all", "common.all", "", "layout-grid"], ["committee", "committee.events.f_committee", meetings.length, "users"], ["neta", "committee.events.f_neta", nNeta, "map-pin"], ["calendar", "committee.events.f_calendar", nCal, "grapes"]] %}
      {%- if f[0] == "all" or f[2] %}
      <button type="button" class="chip" data-cm-filter="{{ f[0] }}" @click="set('{{ f[0] }}')" :aria-pressed="(filter === '{{ f[0] }}').toString()" aria-pressed="{{ 'true' if f[0] == 'all' else 'false' }}">
        {% icon f[3], "size-4" %} {{ f[1] | t(lang) }}{% if f[2] !== "" %} <span class="cm-chip-count">{{ f[2] }}</span>{% endif %}
      </button>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    {% if months | length > 1 %}
    <nav class="flex min-w-0 max-w-full items-center gap-2.5" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.months_aria' | t(lang) }}">
      <span class="shrink-0 text-faint" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4" %}</span>
      <ul class="chip-row min-w-0" role="list">
        {%- for grp in months %}
        <li x-show="monthVisible($refs['m{{ grp.key }}']) && (more || !$el.hasAttribute('data-cm-more'))"{% if fold and grp.key >= fold.from %} data-cm-more data-dflt-hidden{% endif %}><a class="chip" href="#month-{{ grp.key }}">{{ grp.items[0].monthShort }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </nav>
    {% endif %}
    {#- the colour key: only the kinds on this page (committee meeting · Grapevine · La Viña · booth · Area event ·
        the grey one), each card's badge says its kind in words too — the pinned Grapevine Meeting and the "every
        week" cards below (#ev-weekly: Grapevine's and La Viña's colours) count as well. The grey kind is "NETA 65"
        when every grey card is one of ours (its badge says so: kindBadge — today the Grapevine Meeting), else
        "Other events". -#}
    {%- set wos = db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll(lang) -%}
    {%- set gm = site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting", lang, db.events.items) -%}
    {%- set toneSrc = upcoming.concat([gm.next] if gm else []) -%}
    {%- for w in wos %}{% set _n = toneSrc.push({ host: "lv" if w.isLv else "gv" }) %}{% endfor -%}
    {%- set kinds = toneSrc | eventToneSet %}
    {%- set greyOthers = [] -%}
    {%- for ev in toneSrc %}{% if ev.group != "neta" and (ev | eventTone) == "other" and greyOthers.push(ev) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    {% if kinds | length > 1 %}
    <div class="ev-legend">
      <span class="ev-legend-label" id="ev-legend-label">{{ "committee.events.legend" | t(lang) }}</span>
      <ul class="ev-legend-list" role="list" aria-labelledby="ev-legend-label">
        {%- for k in kinds %}
        <li class="ev-tone-{{ k }}"><span class="ev-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ ("committee.events.kind." + ("neta" if (k == "other" and not greyOthers.length) else k)) | t(lang) }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
  <p class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" x-text="countText()"></p>

  {#- ---------- Pinned: our monthly meetings (round 30) ----------
      The owner's "sticky": PINNED — always shown, first, whatever the chip (no x-show), never counted (no
      data-group: not a card of the list; the same meetings' dates are cards in the months too — the duplicate is
      meant). Not CSS position: sticky. Its heading "Our monthly meetings" and, with both cards, one line that says
      so; then (1) the next committee meeting — the dark card, the page's FIRST .cm-pinned (tests read its
      settings) — and (2) the next Grapevine Meeting (#ev-next-gvm), built like a weekly open meeting's card. Each
      rolls on in the browser (cmMeeting: the next date once one is over, "Live now" during it, the visitor's own
      time). -#}
  {% if next or gm %}
  <section id="ev-pinned" class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="ev-pinned-title">
    <h2 id="ev-pinned-title" class="cm-month-title">{% icon "pin", "size-5 shrink-0 text-grape" %}{{ "committee.events.pinned_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    {% if next and gm %}<p class="measure -mt-1.5 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "committee.events.pinned_text" | t(lang) }}</p>{% endif %}
    <div class="grid gap-4">
  {% if next %}
  {#- (the guest speakers to come, each with that meeting's calendar text: the card shows the speaker of the date it
      shows — none on a date without one —, also once it rolls on in the browser: committee.js cmSpeakers) -#}
  {%- set spk = site | cmSpeakers(lang) -%}
  {%- set cfg = { rule: m | cmRuleObj, start: next.startIso, end: next.endIso, title: next.title, description: next.calDescription, location: next.calLocation, url: ('/meetings/#committee-meeting' | lurl(lang) | siteUrl(site)), speakers: spk.list, plain: spk.plain, i18n: { join: "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, pf), soon: "committee.meeting.join_soon" | t(lang), live: "committee.meeting.join_live" | t(lang), yourTime: "committee.meeting.your_time" | t(lang), speaker: "committee.meeting.speaker" | t(lang) } } -%}
  <article class="cm-pinned @container" x-data="cmMeeting({{ cfg | json }})" aria-labelledby="ev-next-title">
    <div class="cm-pinned-grid">
      <div class="cm-date-tile cm-tone-light" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="cm-tile-mon" x-text="tile.mon">{{ next.tile.mon }}</span>
        <span class="cm-tile-day" x-text="tile.day">{{ next.tile.day }}</span>
        <span class="cm-tile-wd" x-text="tile.wd">{{ next.tile.wd }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-white/75">
          {% icon "pin", "size-3.5" %}
          <span x-show="phase === 'upcoming'">{{ "committee.events.pinned_next" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span x-show="phase !== 'upcoming'" x-cloak class="inline-flex items-center gap-2"><span class="cm-live-dot"></span>{{ "committee.meeting.live_now" | t(lang) }}</span>
        </p>
        <h3 id="ev-next-title" class="mt-1.5 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-white">{{ next.title }}</h3>
        <p class="mt-1.5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-white/80">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} <span x-text="dateLabel">{{ next.dateLabel }}</span></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4" %} <span x-text="timeLabel">{{ next.timeLabel }}</span></span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ pf.platform }}</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-white/65" x-show="localLabel" x-text="localLabel" x-cloak></p>
        {% if spk.list | length %}
        <p class="mt-2 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-white/85" x-show="speaker"{% if not next.speaker %} x-cloak{% endif %}>
          {% icon "mic", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0" %}
          <span class="min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-white" x-text="speakerLine">{{ ("committee.meeting.speaker" | t(lang, { name: next.speaker.name })) if next.speaker }}</span><span x-show="speaker && speaker.topic"> — “<span x-text="speaker ? speaker.topic : ''">{{ next.speaker.topic if next.speaker }}</span>”</span></span>
        </p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="cm-pinned-actions">
        <a href="{{ next.online or m.online_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-light btn-sm" :class="phase !== 'upcoming' && 'cm-join-live'">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} <span x-text="joinText">{{ "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, pf) }}</span></a>
        <details class="cm-menu">
          <summary class="btn-on-dark btn-sm">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} {{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</summary>
          <div class="cm-menu-panel cm-menu-right">
            <a :href="gcal" href="{{ next.gcal }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar</a>
            <a :href="outlook" href="{{ next.outlook }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Outlook.com</a>
            <button type="button" @click="downloadIcs()" data-cm-js>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <p class="cm-menu-note" data-cm-js>{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a href="{{ '/meetings/' | lurl(lang) }}#committee-meeting" class="btn-on-dark btn-sm">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
  {% endif %}

  {#- (2) The next Grapevine Meeting: site | cmSeriesNext("grapevine-meeting") (set with the colour key above — worked
      out from the settings, so it is right before the data sync lists it; null: no such series or no date to come,
      no card). Built like a weekly open meeting's card (#ev-weekly below) in its own grey (ev-tone-other: ours, never
      Grapevine's colour — its badge says NETA 65, with the camera: online only): "Every month", "In English" unless
      its title says so ("Reunión de Grapevine (en inglés)"), the title, the rule and time, "Online on Google Meet",
      then the next date — cmMeeting (the /meetings/#grapevine-meeting countdown's settings, gmCfg: the UID
      /events.ics gives each date, so adding it twice keeps one entry; `first`: "First meeting:" on the series'
      first date) rolls it on, says "Live now" during the meeting and adds the visitor's own time. Join on Google
      Meet (its full link; a screen reader hears which meeting), Meeting details (/meetings/#grapevine-meeting: the
      meeting code, what happens), Add to calendar (Google / Outlook links of the date shown, the .ics file) and its
      flyer (the date's, from events.json: View flyer and the tile from 640px; none without one). Phones: Join on its
      own row, Details and Calendar side by side with their short words, View flyer on a row of its own. -#}
  {% if gm %}
  {%- set gmPf = { platform: gm.join.platform } -%}
  {%- set gmJoin = ("committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, gmPf)) if gm.join.platform else ("committee.events.join_online" | t(lang)) -%}
  {%- set gmCfg = {
    rule: gm.rule, start: gm.next.startIso, end: gm.next.endIso, title: gm.next.title, description: gm.next.calDescription,
    location: gm.next.calLocation, url: gm.next.detailsUrl, uid: gm.uidPrefix, file: "grapevine-meeting-", first: gm.starts,
    i18n: { join: gmJoin, soon: "committee.meeting.join_soon" | t(lang), live: "committee.meeting.join_live" | t(lang), yourTime: "committee.meeting.your_time" | t(lang) }
  } -%}
  {%- set gmFirst = gm.next.startYmd == gm.starts -%}
  <article id="ev-next-gvm" class="card ev-accent ev-tone-other cm-event" x-data="cmMeeting({{ gmCfg | json }})" aria-labelledby="ev-next-gvm-title">
    <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
        {{ kindBadge(gm.next, "other") }}
        <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_recurring" | t(lang) }}</span>
        {% if not gm.saysLang %}<span class="badge-muted">{% icon "languages", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.weekly.lang_en" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
      </div>
      <h3 id="ev-next-gvm-title" class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">{{ gm.title }}</h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
        <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "repeat", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ gm.recurrenceDay }} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {{ gm.time }}</span></li>
        <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ ("committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, gmPf)) if gm.join.platform else ("committee.events.online" | t(lang)) }}</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-2.5 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted">
        {% icon "calendar", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}
        <span class="min-w-0">
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase === 'live'" x-cloak>{{ "committee.meeting.live_now" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase !== 'live' && isFirst"{% if not gmFirst %} x-cloak{% endif %}>{{ "committee.events.first_meeting" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink" x-show="phase !== 'live' && !isFirst"{% if gmFirst %} x-cloak{% endif %}>{{ "committee.weekly.next" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span x-text="dateLabel">{{ gm.next.dateLabel }}</span> <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> <span x-text="timeLabel">{{ gm.next.timeLabel }}</span>
          <span class="block text-xs" x-show="localLabel" x-text="localLabel" x-cloak></span>
        </span>
      </p>
      <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,9.5rem),1fr))] gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap">
        {% if gm.join.url %}<a class="btn-primary btn-sm col-span-full" href="{{ gm.join.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" :class="phase !== 'upcoming' && 'cm-join-live'">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} <span x-text="joinText">{{ gmJoin }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }} ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>{% endif %}
        <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ '/meetings/#grapevine-meeting' | lurl(lang) }}">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.details_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ gm.title }}</span></a>
        <details class="cm-menu">
          <summary class="btn-secondary btn-sm w-full sm:w-auto">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.cal_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</span> {% icon "chevron-down", "size-4 opacity-70" %}</summary>
          <div class="cm-menu-panel max-sm:right-0 max-sm:left-auto">
            <a :href="gcal" href="{{ gm.next.gcal }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar</a>
            <a :href="outlook" href="{{ gm.next.outlook }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Outlook.com</a>
            <button type="button" @click="downloadIcs()" data-cm-js>{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <p class="cm-menu-note" data-cm-js>{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
        {{ ui.flyerButton(gm.next.flyer, gm.title, lang, "btn-secondary btn-sm col-span-full") }}
      </div>
    </div>
    {{ ui.flyerThumb(gm.next.flyer, gm.title, lang) }}
  </article>
  {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Every week: the weekly open meetings, under our pinned monthly meetings (#ev-pinned) ----------
      AA Grapevine's Weekly Open (Wednesdays, in English) and La Viña's Reunión Abierta (Thursdays, in Spanish):
      db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll, the page language's first — the meetings, dates and calendar files of
      /meetings/#weekly-open, their one home. Not entries of events.json: a date every week would fill the months
      below, the /events.ics feed, Home's "Upcoming events" and the monthly e-mail. Shown with "All" and the GV & LV
      calendars; not an li[data-group], so the chips, "Showing N" and the month list never count it (without
      JavaScript it shows). Each card, in its magazine's colour (ev-tone-gv / -lv, kindBadge's "Grapevine" /
      "La Viña"): "Every week", its language, the title, the day and time (Central · the host's), the next date —
      the /meetings/ cards' data-cm-weekly markup, so committee.js weekly() rolls it on, says "Live now" and adds the
      visitor's own time; before La Viña's first meeting it says "Starts Thursday, November 5, 2026" —, then Join on
      Zoom, Meeting details, Add to calendar and View flyer. Join on Zoom is the meeting's full Zoom link (w.zoomUrl:
      with its "?pwd=…", nobody types the passcode), the /meetings/ cards' button and label (committee.weekly.join_gv
      / _lv name the meeting). Meeting details leads to /meetings/#weekly-open: the Zoom ID, passcode, joining by
      phone and the recordings are there. Add to calendar: every week, Google's link and the .ics file of /meetings/
      (plain links, no JavaScript needed; both carry the full link). The meeting's official flyer (cmWeeklyFlyer:
      the /meetings/ card's, from its settings' flyer_match) as on every event card: View flyer, and the tile beside
      the text from 640px (ui.flyerButton / ui.flyerThumb; none without a flyer). Phones: Join on its own row, then
      the other two side by side when both fit, with their short words ("Details", "Calendar"; a screen reader hears
      the whole label) — the calendar menu then opens to the left, so it stays on screen — View flyer on a row of its
      own when it is the odd one; else one under the other; from 640px one row. -#}
  {#- (wos: set above, with the colour key) -#}
  {% if wos | length %}
  <section id="ev-weekly" class="mb-10" x-show="filter === 'all' || filter === 'calendar'" aria-labelledby="ev-weekly-title">
    <h2 id="ev-weekly-title" class="cm-month-title">{{ "committee.weekly.section_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <p class="measure -mt-1.5 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "committee.events.weekly_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <ul class="grid gap-4" role="list">
      {% for w in wos %}
      {%- set key = "lv" if w.isLv else "gv" -%}
      {%- set wTitle = w.title or ("committee.weekly.title" | t(lang)) -%}
      {%- set wf = w | cmWeeklyFlyer(site, db.drive.items) -%}
      <li>
        <article class="card ev-accent ev-tone-{{ key }} cm-event" aria-labelledby="ev-weekly-{{ key }}">
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              {{ kindBadge({}, key) }}
              <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</span>
              <span class="badge-muted">{% icon "languages", "size-3" %} {{ ("committee.weekly.lang_" + w.lang) | t(lang) }}</span>
            </div>
            <h3 id="ev-weekly-{{ key }}" class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">{{ wTitle }}</h3>
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {%- set whenParts = [w.day, w.timeCentral, w.hostTime] | select %}
              {% if whenParts | length %}
              <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{% for part in whenParts %}{% if not loop.first %} <span aria-hidden="true">·</span> {% endif %}{{ part }}{% endfor %}</span></li>
              {% endif %}
              <li class="inline-flex items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <span class="min-w-0">{{ "committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, { platform: "Zoom" }) }}</span></li>
            </ul>
            {% if w.next %}
            <p class="mt-2.5 flex items-start gap-1.5 text-sm text-muted" data-cm-weekly="{{ w.next.iso }}" data-cm-weekly-tz="{{ w.next.tz }}"{% if w.next.at %} data-cm-weekly-at="{{ w.next.at }}"{% endif %}{% if w.starts %} data-cm-weekly-starts="{{ w.starts.iso }}"{% endif %} data-cm-weekly-len="60">
              {% icon "calendar", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}
              <span class="min-w-0">
                {%- if w.starts %}
                <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-cm-weekly-label data-next="{{ 'committee.weekly.next' | t(lang) }}" data-live="{{ 'committee.meeting.live_now' | t(lang) }}">{{ "committee.weekly.starts" | t(lang, { date: w.starts.date }) }}</span>
                <span data-cm-weekly-date>· {{ w.starts.range }}</span>
                {%- else %}
                <span class="font-semibold text-ink" data-cm-weekly-label data-next="{{ 'committee.weekly.next' | t(lang) }}" data-live="{{ 'committee.meeting.live_now' | t(lang) }}">{{ "committee.weekly.next" | t(lang) }}</span>
                <span data-cm-weekly-date>{{ w.next.date }} · {{ w.next.range }}</span>
                {%- endif %}
                <span class="block text-xs" data-cm-weekly-local data-tpl="{{ 'committee.meeting.your_time' | t(lang) }}" hidden></span>
              </span>
            </p>
            {% endif %}
            {%- set wc = w | cmWeeklyCal(site, lang) %}
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,9.5rem),1fr))] gap-2 sm:flex sm:flex-wrap">
              {% if w.zoomUrl %}<a class="btn-primary btn-sm col-span-full" href="{{ w.zoomUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ ('committee.weekly.join_' + key) | t(lang) }}">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, { platform: "Zoom" }) }}</a>{% endif %}
              <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ '/meetings/#weekly-open' | lurl(lang) }}">{% icon "info", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.details_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.meeting_details" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> — {{ wTitle }}</span></a>
              {% if wc %}
              <details class="cm-menu">
                <summary class="btn-secondary btn-sm w-full sm:w-auto" aria-label="{{ 'committee.weekly.cal_aria' | t(lang, { name: wTitle }) }}">{% icon "calendar-plus", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden">{{ "committee.events.cal_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:hidden">{{ "common.add_to_calendar" | t(lang) }}</span> {% icon "chevron-down", "size-4 opacity-70" %}</summary>
                <div class="cm-menu-panel max-sm:right-0 max-sm:left-auto">
                  <a href="{{ wc.gcal }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "calendar", "size-4" %} Google Calendar<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
                  <a href="{{ wc.ics }}" download="weekly-open-{{ wc.key }}.ics" type="text/calendar">{% icon "download", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.cal.ics_file" | t(lang) }}</a>
                  <p class="cm-menu-note">{{ "committee.cal.reminder_timed" | t(lang) }}</p>
                </div>
              </details>
              {% endif %}
              {{ ui.flyerButton(wf, wTitle, lang, "btn-secondary btn-sm" + (" col-span-full" if wc else "")) }}
            </div>
          </div>
          {{ ui.flyerThumb(wf, wTitle, lang) }}
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Upcoming, grouped by month ----------
      Every date to come, a card each (a monthly series' every date, every committee meeting). A folded month (fold,
      above: a year after the open ones) carries data-cm-more + data-dflt-hidden and shows once
      "Show {range} dates (n)" is pressed (cmEvents `more`); its heading takes the keyboard then (tabindex="-1").
      That button comes right after the last open month: data-js-only (without JavaScript every month shows), shown
      while a folded card the chip picked is hidden, with that chip's count (moreCount; the build writes the "All"
      count, n of fold). -#}
  {% for grp in months %}
  {%- set folded = fold and grp.key >= fold.from %}
  {% if folded and grp.key == fold.keys[0] %}
  <div class="cm-ev-more" data-js-only x-show="!more && moreCount">
    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" @click="showMore()">{% icon "chevron-down", "size-4" %} <span data-label="{{ 'committee.events.show_more' | t(lang, { range: fold.range }) }}" x-text="moreText($el)">{{ "committee.events.show_more" | t(lang, { range: fold.range, n: fold.n }) }}</span></button>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <section class="cm-month" data-cm-month x-ref="m{{ grp.key }}" x-show="monthVisible($el) && (more || !$el.hasAttribute('data-cm-more'))"{% if folded %} data-cm-more data-dflt-hidden{% endif %} aria-labelledby="month-{{ grp.key }}">
    <h2 id="month-{{ grp.key }}" class="cm-month-title"{% if folded %} tabindex="-1"{% endif %}>{{ grp.items[0].monthLabel }}</h2>
    <ol class="grid gap-4">
      {% for ev in grp.items %}
      {%- set kind = ev | eventTone %}
      {#- Share: the event's own small page (src/pages/event-share.11ty.js), whose link preview shows its title, day
          and flyer — it leads on to this card; a committee meeting's card is shared as it is -#}
      {%- set shareUrl = (pageAbs + "#" + ev.anchor) if ev.committee else (("/events/" + ev.anchor + "/") | lurl(lang) | siteUrl(site)) %}
      {#- data-group: the filter chips it shows under — one group, or "committee neta" for a committee meeting (a
          NETA 65 event too: cmEvents reads the list; ev.group itself stays "committee" for every other page) -#}
      <li id="{{ ev.anchor }}" data-group="{{ ev.group }}{{ ' neta' if ev.committee }}" data-cm-expire="{{ ev.expireIso }}" x-show="show($el)">
        <article class="card cm-event ev-accent ev-tone-{{ kind }}">
          {#- the date: a tile column from 640px; on a phone a strip above the title (+ Share as an icon) -#}
          <div class="cm-date-tile{{ ' cm-tile-range' if ev.tile.range }} max-sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="cm-tile-mon">{{ ev.tile.mon }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-day">{{ ev.tile.day }}</span>
            <span class="cm-tile-wd">{{ ev.tile.wd }}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
            <div class="mb-2.5 flex items-center justify-between gap-3 sm:hidden">
              <p class="cm-date-strip" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "calendar", "size-3.5" %}<span>{{ ev.tile.wd }} · {{ ev.tile.mon }} {{ ev.tile.day }}</span></p>
              <button type="button" class="btn-ghost -my-1 -mr-2 size-11 shrink-0 p-0" data-js-only data-share="{{ shareUrl }}" data-share-title="{{ ev.title }}" data-share-text="{{ ev.shareWhen }}" aria-label="{{ 'common.share' | t(lang) }}: {{ ev.title }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %}</button>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
              {{ kindBadge(ev, kind) }}
              {% if ev.tentative %}{{ ui.tentativeBadge(lang) }}{% endif %}
              {% if ev.recurring %}<span class="badge-muted">{% icon "repeat", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.events.badge_recurring" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.isNew %}<span class="badge-new">{{ "common.new" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
              {% if not ev.committee and not ev.ownWords %}{{ ui.langPill(ev.item, lang) }}{% endif %}
            </div>
            <h3 class="h-card mt-2 text-lg sm:text-xl">
              {%- if ev.link and ev.link != (ev.flyer.view if ev.flyer else "") -%}
              <a href="{{ ev.link }}" class="-my-3 inline-block py-3 hover:text-gv"{% if ev.linkExternal %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{{ ev.title }}</a>
              {%- else -%}{{ ev.title }}{%- endif -%}
            </h3>
            {#- the tile is hidden from screen readers: the date is read here (a range is in the list below) -#}
            {% if not ev.multiDay %}<p class="sr-only">{{ ev.dateLabel }}</p>{% endif %}
            <ul class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1 text-sm text-muted">
              {#- Several days (an Area assembly): the date range; the tile shows it too -#}
              {% if ev.multiDay %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-medium text-ink">{% icon "calendar-range", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.rangeLabel }}</li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.timeLabel %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "clock-3", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.timeLabel }}</li>{% endif %}
              {#- A place not known yet ("Venue to be announced"): plain italic text, no map pin -#}
              {% if ev.location and ev.locationTba %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 italic">{% icon "hourglass", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.location }}</li>
              {% elif ev.location %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% set locIcon = "video" if ev.committee else "map-pin" %}{% icon locIcon, "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.location }}</li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.isOnline %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "video", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ("committee.events.online_on" | t(lang, { platform: ev.platform })) if ev.platform else ("committee.events.online" | t(lang)) }}</li>{% endif %}
              {#- the meeting ID or code to type into the meeting app (recurring_events `meeting_id:` — "Meeting code" for
                  a Google Meet code: ev.meetingIdKey); "Join online" opens the link.
                  inline-block: with larger text on a phone (where no-wrap is lifted) the number moves to the next
                  line in one piece instead of breaking after "815" -#}
              {% if ev.meetingId %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "hash", "size-4 text-faint" %} <span>{{ ev.meetingIdKey | t(lang) }} <span class="inline-block whitespace-nowrap font-mono font-medium text-ink" translate="no">{{ ev.meetingId }}</span></span></li>{% endif %}
              {#- who to write to (recurring_events `contact:`): a line of its own, so the address never hides in the
                  3 lines the card shows of the summary; tap-link: 44px tall on phones; @<wbr> lets a long address
                  wrap after the "@" with larger text (it is checked to be a plain e-mail address: committee.js) -#}
              {% if ev.contact %}<li class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "mail", "size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %} <a class="link tap-link min-w-0 break-words" href="mailto:{{ ev.contact }}" translate="no"><span class="sr-only">{{ "committee.events.contact" | t(lang) }}: </span>{{ ev.contact | replace("@", "@<wbr>") | safe }}</a></li>{% endif %}
              {% if ev.recurrenceDay %}<li class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">{% icon "repeat", "size-4 text-faint" %} {{ ev.recurrenceDay }}</li>{% endif %}
              {#- a committee meeting's guest speaker and topic (committee.js normalizeEvents: ev.speaker — never in what
                  search engines read) -#}
              {% if ev.speaker %}<li class="flex min-w-0 basis-full items-start gap-1.5">{% icon "mic", "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 text-faint" %}<span class="min-w-0"><span class="font-medium text-ink">{{ "committee.meeting.speaker" | t(lang, { name: ev.speaker.name }) }}</span>{% if ev.speaker.topic %} — “{{ ev.speaker.topic }}”{% endif %}</span></li>{% endif %}
            </ul>
            {% if not ev.committee %}
            {%- set foreign = not ev.ownWords and ev.item.lang and ev.item.lang != lang and ev.item.lang != "und" and not (ev.item | machineFor(lang)) -%}
            {% if ev.body %}
            {#- the card's title is an h3: the description's own headings start at h4, its links to our pages go to
                this language's page, each table is named after the event (md: eleventy.config.js); cm-md
                (committee.css) styles its headings, tables, lists and quotes, as on the bulletin -#}
            <div class="prose-site cm-md mt-3 max-w-none text-[0.95rem]"{% if foreign %} lang="{{ ev.item.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ ev.body | md({ h: 4, lang: lang, name: ev.title }) | safe }}</div>
            {% elif ev.summary %}
            <p class="mt-2.5 line-clamp-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted"{% if foreign %} lang="{{ ev.item.lang }}"{% endif %}>{{ ev.summary | excerpt(280) }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if ev.item | machineFor(lang) %}<p class="mt-1.5">{{ ui.autoNote(ev.item, lang) }}</p>{% endif %}
            {% endif %}
            {#- phones: a two-column grid of equal buttons (an odd last one spans both); from 640px one row,
                with Share at its end (on a narrow card it wraps with the last button, never alone on a row:
                committee.css .cm-ev-actions). "Event details" is a button only when there is no flyer — otherwise
                the title is that link, so the actions stay two. -#}
            <div class="cm-ev-actions">
              <div class="cm-ev-btns">
              {% if ev.committee %}
              <a class="btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.online }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "video", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.meeting.join" | t(lang, pf) }}<span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
              {% elif ev.online %}
              <a class="btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.online }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "globe", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.join_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.join_online" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
              {% endif %}
              {{ calMenu(ev) }}
              {{ ui.flyerButton(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang) }}
              {% if ev.link and ev.linkExternal and not ev.flyer %}
              <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" href="{{ ev.link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "external-link", "size-4" %} <span class="sm:hidden" aria-hidden="true">{{ "committee.events.details_short" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="max-sm:sr-only">{{ "committee.events.details" | t(lang) }}</span><span class="sr-only"> ({{ "common.external" | t(lang) }})</span></a>
              {% endif %}
              </div>
              <button type="button" class="btn-ghost btn-sm max-xl:px-2.5 max-sm:hidden" data-js-only data-share="{{ shareUrl }}" data-share-title="{{ ev.title }}" data-share-text="{{ ev.shareWhen }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %}<span class="max-xl:sr-only">{{ "common.share" | t(lang) }}</span></button>
            </div>
          </div>
          {#- The flyer on the side (from 640px; on a phone the "View flyer" button above is the way to it):
              EVERY event with a flyer has this tile — the same link and preview as "View flyer" (ui.flyerThumb:
              its picture, else the tile's own flyer icon and the word "Flyer", never an empty space) -#}
          {{ ui.flyerThumb(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang) }}
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {#- ---------- Empty states ---------- -#}
  {#- (no event of OUR OWN: the committee meetings, NETA 65 events too, are not what this is about) -#}
  {% if nNetaOwn == 0 %}
  {#- No flyers / manual events yet: one line for visitors + a pointer to the committee how-to
      (the naming rule and the Drive folder are in "For committee members · Add an event", #how-events) -#}
  <div id="ev-empty-neta" class="mt-2" x-show="filter === 'all' || filter === 'neta'">
    {{ ui.emptyState("calendar-days", "committee.events.empty_neta_title" | t(lang), "committee.events.empty_neta_text" | t(lang), "#how-events", "committee.events.how_link" | t(lang)) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if nCal == 0 %}
  <div class="mt-2" x-show="filter === 'calendar'" x-cloak>
    {{ ui.emptyState("grapes", "committee.events.empty_cal_title" | t(lang), "committee.events.empty_cal_text" | t(lang), "https://www.aagrapevine.org/get-involved/calendar", "committee.events.empty_cal_cta" | t(lang)) }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- Past events ---------- -#}
  {% if past | length %}
  <details class="card mt-12 group/past" data-cm-past>
    <summary class="flex min-h-14 cursor-pointer list-none items-center gap-3 px-5 py-4 sm:px-6">
      <span class="grid size-10 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-surface-2 text-muted">{% icon "history", "size-5" %}</span>
      <h2 class="h-card flex-1 text-lg">{{ "committee.events.past" | t(lang) }} <span class="font-sans text-sm font-normal text-muted">({{ past | length }})</span></h2>
      {% icon "chevron-down", "size-5 text-muted transition group-open/past:rotate-180" %}
    </summary>
    <ol class="divide-y divide-line border-t border-line">
      {% for ev in past | limit(40) %}
      <li id="{{ ev.anchor }}" class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-1 px-5 py-3.5 sm:px-6">
        <time class="inline-flex w-32 shrink-0 items-center gap-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-muted" datetime="{{ ev.startIso }}"><span class="ev-dot ev-tone-{{ ev | eventTone }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ ev.startIso | fmtDate(lang, "short") }}</time>
        <span class="min-w-[11rem] flex-1 break-words font-medium text-ink">{{ ev.title }}{% if ev.location and not ev.locationTba %} <span class="text-sm font-normal text-muted">· {{ ev.location }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
        {% if ev.flyer %}{{ ui.flyerButton(ev.flyer, ev.title, lang, "btn-ghost btn-sm") }}
        {% elif ev.link and ev.linkExternal %}<a class="btn-ghost btn-sm" href="{{ ev.link }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "external-link", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.events.details" | t(lang) }}</a>{% endif %}
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </details>
  {% endif %}

  {#- ---------- How events get here (the three kinds of events, in visitors' words; how the
       committee adds one is in "For committee members · Add an event" below) ---------- -#}
  <section class="panel-muted mt-12" aria-labelledby="ev-src-title">
    <h2 id="ev-src-title" class="card-h"><span>{% icon "sparkles", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "committee.events.sources_title" | t(lang) }}</h2>
    <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-muted">{{ "committee.events.sources_sub" | t(lang) }}</p>
    <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {% for s in [["meetings", "users", "bg-grape-soft text-grape"], ["flyers", "map-pin", "bg-vine-soft text-vine"], ["calendars", "grapes", "bg-lv-soft text-lv"]] %}
      <li class="flex gap-3.5">
        <span class="grid size-10 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl {{ s[2] }}">{% icon s[1], "size-5" %}</span>
        <div class="min-w-0">
          <h3 class="h-card text-base">{{ ("committee.events.src_" + s[0]) | t(lang) }}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ ("committee.events.src_" + s[0] + "_text") | t(lang, pf) }}</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>
</section>

{#- ---------- Sidebar: the calendar subscription, then "Next 5 weeks" ----------
     From 1024px a column beside the agenda; below 1024px it follows the agenda (DOM order = phone order = Tab
     order: one copy, never moved). First the .ics subscription card (#subscribe: the hero's "Subscribe" button,
     Home and /meetings/ link to it; cmSubscribe, as it was), then the calendar card (#ev-cal). The aside itself is
     NOT sticky — as a grid item it stretches over the whole row —: its inner wrapper is (sticky-aside: from 1024px
     when the window is at least 640px tall, never taller than the window, static at larger text — main.css), and a
     sticky box can't leave its parent (digest.njk's rule): the feed card scrolls away with the page, then the
     calendar stays in view under the header while the list scrolls by, to the end of the agenda. (A sticky aside
     holding both was taller than most windows: the calendar sat in its faded inner scroll.)
     "Next 5 weeks" (cmCalWeeks → committee.js calendarWeeks, where every rule is explained): a month-style grid,
     Sunday first, of the five weeks from this one (Central time) — EVERY upcoming event of the list on each of its
     days (committee meetings, each date of a monthly series, an assembly on all its days) and the two weekly open
     meetings — plus three spare weeks, hidden: as each week ends, the browser drops its row and shows the next
     (committee.js expire(): the row's data-cm-expire is the moment its Saturday ends; the tbody's data-cm-max="5"
     shows the first five rows left, as the meeting dates on /meetings/), so five weeks always show between builds.
     A plain table (not role="grid"): Tab goes through the days that have something on, row by row, and a screen
     reader names each column's weekday. Each such day is a link to its first event's card in the list (without
     JavaScript that is where it goes) holding the day's number, the whole day in words for screen readers ("Wednesday,
     November 18: Committee meeting, 7:00 PM; …") and up to 3 dots in the events' colours (a weekly meeting's: a ring;
     more: "+n"); a day with nothing on is its number; the 1st of a month (and the grid's first day) names its month.
     The build's today: .is-today + aria-current="date"; the days before it: .is-past, no link.
     Under the grid, the day's list (aria-live: read out when it changes): each day with something on has its own,
     hidden but one — today's when something is on today, else the next day with something on ("Next up"). Its
     heading is the date, each entry its colour's dot, its time (Central) and its title, a link to its card
     (#ev-weekly-gv / -lv for the weekly meetings: "Every week"). With JavaScript, picking a day shows that day's list
     (.is-selected on the day) instead of jumping; a link to a card the list hides (another chip, a month folded
     behind "Show more") is revealed by the list itself (cmEvents: on hashchange, and on "cm:reveal" when the link
     goes to the hash already in the address). Every minute committee.js calToday() moves today and the past
     days on (a page left open, or an offline copy), dims what is over and keeps the month caption right.
     Then the colour key of the dots (only the colours used; "Every week": the ring) and one line of help.
     data-lastmod="skip": the card changes with the day, not with the content (eleventy/lastmod.js). No card when
     nothing is on in these weeks (calendarWeeks: null). -#}
<aside class="min-w-0" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.aside_aria' | t(lang) }}">
  <div id="subscribe">
    {% cmSubscribe lang, site %}
  </div>
  {%- set cal = upcoming | cmCalWeeks(db.weekly_open.items | cmWeeklyAll(lang), lang, { weeks: 5, spare: 3 }) %}
  {% if cal %}
  <div class="sticky-aside mt-6">
    <section id="ev-cal" class="cm-cal-card card card-pad" data-cm-cal data-lastmod="skip" aria-labelledby="ev-cal-title">
      <p class="eyebrow text-gv">{{ "committee.events.cal_eyebrow" | t(lang) }}</p>
      <h2 id="ev-cal-title" class="card-h mt-2"><span>{% icon "calendar-days", "size-5" %}</span>{{ "committee.events.cal_title" | t(lang, { n: cal.n }) }}</h2>
      <p class="cm-cal-cap" data-cm-cal-cap="{{ cal.captionFrom }}">{{ cal.caption }}</p>
      <table class="cm-cal" aria-labelledby="ev-cal-title">
        <thead>
          <tr>{% for wd in cal.weekdays %}<th scope="col"><span class="cm-cal-wd" aria-hidden="true">{{ wd.short }}</span><span class="cm-cal-wd2" aria-hidden="true">{{ wd.tiny }}</span><span class="sr-only">{{ wd.long }}</span></th>{% endfor %}</tr>
        </thead>
        {#- (whitespace control throughout: 56 cells and a list per day add up) -#}
        <tbody data-cm-max="{{ cal.n }}">
          {%- for wk in cal.weeks -%}
          <tr data-cm-expire="{{ wk.endIso }}"{% if wk.hidden %} class="hidden"{% endif %}>
            {%- for d in wk.days -%}
            <td class="cm-cal-d{{ ' is-today' if d.today }}{{ ' is-past' if d.past }}{{ ' is-selected' if d.ymd == cal.panel }}" data-cm-day="{{ d.ymd }}"{% if d.today %} aria-current="date"{% endif %}>
              {%- if d.events | length -%}
              <a class="cm-cal-link"{% if not d.past %} href="#{{ d.first }}"{% endif %} data-cm-cal-day="{{ d.ymd }}">{% if d.mon %}<span class="cm-cal-mon" aria-hidden="true">{{ d.mon }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="cm-cal-n" aria-hidden="true">{{ d.day }}</span><span class="sr-only">{{ d.sr }}</span><span class="cm-cal-dots" aria-hidden="true">{% for e in d.dots %}<span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ e.tone }}{{ ' is-weekly' if e.weekly }}"></span>{% endfor %}{% if d.more %}<span class="cm-cal-more">+{{ d.more }}</span>{% endif %}</span></a>
              {%- else -%}
              <span class="cm-cal-day">{% if d.mon %}<span class="cm-cal-mon">{{ d.mon }}</span>{% endif %}{{ d.day }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </td>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </tr>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="cm-cal-panels" aria-live="polite" data-cm-cal-panels data-today="{{ 'common.today' | t(lang) }}" data-next="{{ 'committee.events.cal_next_up' | t(lang) }}">
        {%- for wk in cal.weeks %}{% for d in wk.days %}{% if d.events | length -%}
        <div class="cm-cal-panel" data-cm-cal-panel="{{ d.ymd }}"{% if d.ymd != cal.panel %} hidden{% endif %}>
          <h3 class="cm-cal-ph"><span class="cm-cal-tag" data-cm-cal-tag>{% if d.ymd == cal.panel %}{{ ("common.today" if cal.panelToday else "committee.events.cal_next_up") | t(lang) }}{% endif %}</span> {{ d.label }}</h3>
          <ul class="cm-cal-list" role="list">
            {%- for e in d.events -%}
            <li data-cm-cal-end="{{ e.endIso }}"><span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ e.tone }}{{ ' is-weekly' if e.weekly }}"></span><span>{% if e.time %}<span class="cm-cal-time">{{ e.time }}</span> {% endif %}<a class="cm-cal-ev" href="#{{ e.anchor }}">{{ e.title }}</a>{% if e.weekly %} <span class="cm-cal-wk">· {{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}</span></li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
        {%- endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <ul class="cm-cal-key" role="list" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.legend' | t(lang) }}">
        {%- for k in cal.kinds %}
        <li><span class="cm-cal-dot ev-tone-{{ k.tone }}"></span>{{ k.label }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- if cal.weekly %}
        <li><span class="cm-cal-dot is-weekly"></span>{{ "committee.events.badge_weekly" | t(lang) }}</li>
        {%- endif %}
      </ul>
      <p class="cm-cal-help">{{ "committee.events.cal_help" | t(lang) }}</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</aside>
</div>
</div>

{#- ---------- For committee members (collapsed): add an event — the two kinds of flyers in the same Drive
     folder: a name that starts with a date makes a new event; the flyer of an event already written in
     content/events gets a name WITHOUT a date and is linked from that file (`flyer:`), because a dated flyer
     and a file are never taken for the same event — dated, the event would be listed twice
     (content/events/README.md, "The flyer"). Then the folder, the naming rule with an example of each, and
     the two Drive actions (the same as the Portfolio's) ---------- -#}
{%- set exDate = "2027-03-14" | fmtDate(lang, "medium") -%}
<div class="container-page mt-12">
  {% call ui.memberHelp(lang, "committee.events.how_title" | t(lang), { id: "how-events" }) %}
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)] lg:gap-10">
    <div class="cm-ev-how">
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "committee.events.how_new_q" | t(lang) }}</strong> {{ "committee.events.how_text" | t(lang) }}</p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="font-semibold text-ink">{{ "committee.events.how_linked_q" | t(lang) }}</strong> {{ "committee.events.how_linked" | t(lang, { folder: "<code>content/events</code>", line: "<code>flyer:</code>" }) | safe }}</p>
      {% cmDrivePath lang, di, "flyers" %}
      {% if nNetaOwn == 0 %}{% cmDriveChecked lang, di %}{% endif %}
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
        {% if di.url %}<a class="btn-primary" href="{{ di.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "folder-open", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.drive.open_folder" | t(lang) }}</a>{% endif %}
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="mailto:{{ site.contact_email }}?subject={{ 'committee.docs.mail_subject' | t(lang) | urlencode }}">{% icon "mail", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.docs.ask_access" | t(lang) }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cm-naming-box min-w-0">
      <div class="cm-naming" role="table" aria-label="{{ 'committee.events.naming_aria' | t(lang) }}">
        <div class="cm-naming-head" role="row">
          <span role="columnheader">{{ "committee.events.naming_name" | t(lang) }}</span>
          <span role="columnheader">{{ "committee.events.naming_result" | t(lang) }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex1" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "calendar-check", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex1_out" | t(lang, { date: exDate }) }}</span></span>
        </div>
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex2" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "calendar-check", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex2_out" | t(lang, { date: exDate }) }}</span></span>
        </div>
        {#- no date: no event of its own — the flyer of an event already on the page, linked from its file -#}
        <div class="cm-naming-row" role="row">
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-file">{% icon "file-text", "size-4 shrink-0 text-lv" %}<code>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex3" | t(lang) }}</code></span>
          <span role="cell" class="cm-naming-out">{% icon "link", "size-4 shrink-0 text-vine" %}<span>{{ "committee.events.naming_ex3_out" | t(lang) }}</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ "committee.events.naming_tip" | t(lang) }}</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% cmPreviewDialog lang %}

{#- Structured data (schema.org): the upcoming events held at a place, for search engines' event listings —
    built by cmEventLd (eleventy/filters/committee.js eventLd, where every rule is explained). Google lists only
    events at a physical place with a postal address that the public may attend, so an online-only event (the
    committee meeting, La Viña's Zoom workshop) gets no Event here — this page, the .ics files and the share pages
    still show it; a place not known yet is left out too. A hybrid event (a place AND an `online_url`) is "Mixed",
    with its Place. Each Place has a PostalAddress (street, city, state, ZIP code) read from the event's place;
    the description is its summary, the picture its flyer (else the committee's card), sameAs its own page on
    another site. Only facts we know, no personal names: the organizer is La Viña / Grapevine for their own events
    we share (ev.host), the Area for an Area assembly, nobody for an event from their calendars, else the committee
    (the site's Organization, "#committee"). It stays the page's FIRST ld+json block (tests read that one). -#}
{%- set ldEvents = upcoming | cmEventLd(site, lang, pageAbs) -%}
{% if ldEvents | length %}<script type="application/ld+json">{{ { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": ldEvents } | rpJson | safe }}</script>{% endif %}
